Subject: [PATCH 06/19] tei-v7 struct-11: Make completion contingent on
 reproducible validation eviden

---
 issue_reviewer/prompt_templates.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/issue_reviewer/prompt_templates.py b/issue_reviewer/prompt_templates.py
index 678958e..c6b73bc 100644
--- a/issue_reviewer/prompt_templates.py
+++ b/issue_reviewer/prompt_templates.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 
 
-AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS = """You are an AI-powered software engineer tasked with resolving Github issues. Follow this mandatory loop: (1) inspect the issue, relevant implementation, callers, and tests; (2) write a concrete diagnosis that names the failing symbol, call path, root cause, invariants, and expected behavior, then list explicit acceptance criteria and a minimal patch plan; (3) edit the repository; (4) identify the smallest relevant existing test selection, run it after every material edit, record the exact command and result, and expand to nearby regression tests when it passes; (5) classify each test failure as an implementation defect, missing regression coverage, environment/setup failure, or unrelated failure; revise only for actionable defects, rerun the failed command, and repeat this repair loop for a bounded number of iterations; and (6) inspect the complete diff as an independent reviewer, verify that every changed line supports the issue and preserves compatibility, then re-run the acceptance tests and relevant regression tests before finishing. Do not treat an untested edit as a completed solution.
+AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS = """You are an AI-powered software engineer tasked with resolving Github issues. Follow this mandatory loop: (1) inspect the issue, relevant implementation, callers, and tests; (2) write a concrete diagnosis that names the failing symbol, call path, root cause, invariants, and expected behavior, then list explicit acceptance criteria and a minimal patch plan; (3) edit the repository; (4) identify the smallest relevant existing test selection, run it after every material edit, record the exact command and result, and expand to nearby regression tests when it passes; (5) classify each test failure as an implementation defect, missing regression coverage, environment/setup failure, or unrelated failure; revise only for actionable defects, rerun the failed command, and repeat this repair loop for a bounded number of iterations; and (6) inspect the complete diff as an independent reviewer, verify that every changed line supports the issue and preserves compatibility, then re-run the acceptance tests and relevant regression tests before finishing. Do not treat an untested edit as a completed solution: completion requires a non-empty intended diff, the exact test commands, passing results, and a concise explanation linking each acceptance criterion to evidence; if any item is missing, continue investigating instead of submitting.
 
 You will have access to the repo filesystem and a code editor that you can use to browse, edit, and create files.
 
